   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Differentiate both sides of \\( \\cos\\left(g(x)\\right) = \\frac{- 2 x - 10}{5} \\) with respect to x. The chain rule on the left gives \\( -\\sin\\left(g(x)\\right) \\cdot g'(x) = - \\frac{2}{5} \\).",
         "rule_named": "chain rule on the identity f(g(x)) = x"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Express the trigonometric factor in x by the Pythagorean identity, with the positive root because the sine is not negative on this branch: \\( \\sin\\left(g(x)\\right) = \\sqrt{1 - \\cos^{2}\\left(g(x)\\right)} = \\sqrt{1 - \\left(- \\frac{2 x}{5} - 2\\right)^{2}} \\).",
         "rule_named": "Pythagorean identity on the principal branch"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Solve for the derivative: \\( g'(x) = \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{25 - \\left(- 2 x - 10\\right)^{2}}} \\).",
